{"name":"Midnight Merlot","hex":"#880044","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"midnight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The middle of the night: the sixth temporal hour, equidistant between sunset and sunrise.","Twelve o'clock at night exactly."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Utterly dark or black."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/midnight"},{"term":"merlot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Merlot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/merlot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Midnight","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight is the transition time from one day to the next – the moment when the date changes, on the local official clock time for any particular jurisdiction. By clock time, midnight is the opposite of noon, differing from it by 12 hours."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG/330px-Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight","wikidata":"Q36402"},{"title":"Merlot","blocks":[{"text":"Merlot is a dark-blue-colored wine grape variety that is used as both a blending grape and for varietal wines. The name Merlot is thought to be a diminutive of merle, the French name for the blackbird, probably a reference to the color of the grape. Its softness and \"fleshiness\", combined with its earlier ripening, make Merlot a popular grape for blending with the sterner, later-ripening Cabernet Sauvignon, which tends to be higher in tannin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Merlot.jpg/330px-Merlot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Merlot","wikidata":"Q213338"},{"title":"Midnight blue","blocks":[{"t